    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552">

                <pb facs="0523" n="453" xml:id="pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/299: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-16T18:00:00-06:00">March 16, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Indicative that Mexican Government is watching Guatemala Conference
                    developments closely is information today from Foreign Office that Mexican
                    Legation here has requested Costa Rican reply to General Ubico’s proposals, text
                    of which was not published.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Guatemala.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
